{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all","id":1564829,"title":"Victims: Aren't We All?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-18T20:22:56-07:00","id":1564829,"title":"Victims: Aren't We All?","content":"A place to post your vampire-victims and mortal-NPCs(and not mortal), in general: Here's Isabel Franco (Isi), junkie: She's passed out in the barrens, just laying on the ground. She knows Joe Grubb. If the King of the Homeless shows up, he'll slap her face a few times and tell her she can't lay here. The Flashlight Security-Guard will ignore her. She's good with that pistol (sober). <br /> <br /> <img width=\"1639\" height=\"1062\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://iili.io/nwRre5B.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://iili.io/nwRre5B.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://iili.io/nwRre5B.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T00:09:12-07:00","id":1564834,"title":"","content":"Does she scavenge copper wiring from streetlights too? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T04:44:45-07:00","id":1564836,"title":"","content":"That sheet seems wild for the concept.<br /> <br /> Why she have the Dexterity of a serious national-level athlete?<br /> <br /> Wits and composure well above average?<br /> <br /> Presence 3 + Striking Looks means she's not only very beautiful, but very talented at using it.<br /> <br /> Academics and Computers 2? She could be in college or be a regular professional in those areas. Actually, since its full skill and not Specializations, she could be a very good professional in those areas.<br /> <br /> Dexterity 4 + Wits 3 + Firearms 3 + Weaponry 3 + Gunslinger, she isn't good with that pistol, she's a fucking ninja. She knows how to use any weapon like an expert, can kill you with a BB-gun by hitting your mouth and chocking you, use pistols, rifles or submachine guns like Rambo in the first movie, then move to finish survivors with anything at hand, from katanas to lead pipes, as a pro.<br /> <br /> She's not a victim, she's a high-level assassin with acceptable weaknesses that's down on her luck. Not world-class, but getting there.<br /> <br /> Oh, no, wait, found out why she's like that and still a drunken victim: she talks Spanish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T06:37:13-07:00","id":1564838,"title":"","content":"I'm glad I'm not the only person bothered by this. A person whose entire personality is drugs and robbing people. Less of a tone of &quot;everybody can be victimized, let us humanize the people vampires are forced to feed on&quot; and more of a tone of &quot;it's fun to victimize people like this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T07:03:41-07:00","id":1564840,"title":"","content":"No humanizing victims or marginalized people, and why not be sure a dehumanizing depiction of alcoholism and a bad life is also subtly racist and sexist by making her a hot Chicana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T13:40:00-07:00","id":1564843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564836#post1564836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sheet seems wild for the concept.<br /> <br /> Why she have the Dexterity of a serious national-level athlete?<br /> <br /> Wits and composure well above average?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup; I used <a href=\"https://chronicles-character-builder.app\" target=\"_blank\">https://chronicles-character-builder.app</a>, and that's what came up. The only thing I chose were her merits because they didn't auto-populate. I think I gave her streetwise, because every junkie/homeless person has a little bit of that skill. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Presence 3 + Striking Looks means she's not only very beautiful, but very talented at using it.<br /> <br /> Academics and Computers 2? She could be in college or be a regular professional in those areas. Actually, since its full skill and not Specializations, she could be a very good professional in those areas.<br /> <br /> Dexterity 4 + Wits 3 + Firearms 3 + Weaponry 3 + Gunslinger, she isn't good with that pistol, she's a fucking ninja. She knows how to use any weapon like an expert, can kill you with a BB-gun by hitting your mouth and chocking you, use pistols, rifles or submachine guns like Rambo in the first movie, then move to finish survivors with anything at hand, from katanas to lead pipes, as a pro.<br /> <br /> She's not a victim, she's a high-level assassin with acceptable weaknesses that's down on her luck. Not world-class, but getting there.<br /> <br /> Oh, no, wait, found out why she's like that and still a drunken victim: she talks Spanish. </div> </div> </div>I'm only responsible for the gunslinger and striking-looks merits. I wanted her to take full advantage of her unusually high-stats in those fields. BUT, she's wasting it on opioids. Yeah, she's a drop-out college-student with a lot of potential. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . . .hot chincana </div> </div> </div>; Her name popped-up as Isabel Delgado, but, I wanted to use another last name from another random-name generator. Of course she knows Spanish. <br /> <br /> <br /> I deal with the homeless/junkies, IRL. The no shoes, mental-illness and drug-use are very common.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T15:10:03-07:00","id":1564847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564843#post1564843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I deal with the homeless/junkies, IRL. The no shoes, mental-illness and drug-use are very common.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> They're also people, with a lot more going on them than a stereotype.<br /> <br /> I don't understand how you read so much anthropology and deal with this kind of people IRL and still manage to reduce every culture and group to their simplest stereotypes on your threads. That's not now, it's a pattern.<br /> <br /> And don't think you're the only person in the forums dealing with marginalized people on a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T16:45:24-07:00","id":1564848,"title":"","content":"The Flash Light Security Guard: He's late 20's, wanted to be an actor, but instead, ended up working odd-jobs: he likes using his flashlight because it gives people time to leave when he's patrolling. I rolled 31 XP-points for him. He's put them in to help with all the careers he's had or wanted to have, acting, delivery-driver, and now, night-time, security-guard for an abandoned building in the barrens. <br /> <br /> <img width=\"1616\" height=\"1050\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://iili.io/nwDxJS4.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://iili.io/nwDxJS4.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://iili.io/nwDxJS4.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T18:18:03-07:00","id":1564849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564843#post1564843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup; I used <a href=\"https://chronicles-character-builder.app\" target=\"_blank\">https://chronicles-character-builder.app</a>, and that's what came up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You made a thread for NPC writeups where a large part of the NPC writeup, the dot spreads, are randomly generated rather than something you actually wrote to fit them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T20:45:50-07:00","id":1564852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564849#post1564849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You made a thread for NPC writeups where a large part of the NPC writeup, the dot spreads, are randomly generated rather than something you actually wrote to fit them?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least with actual LLM you bother to give a concept and instructions to the AI.<br /> <br /> Those are random sheets with a stereotype slapped on that doesn't even fit. Now the guy is a failed actor. A failed actor with Presence 3, Expression 3 and Acting. Also a stunt driver at similar level.<br /> <br /> Guy would star Fast and Furious if he were white. Well, at least that part is realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-20T09:52:27-07:00","id":1564871,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stereotypical presentation and dehumanization aside, Chronicles of darkness characters being too good for the type of story it usually seems to want to tell is something I also struggled with.<br /> <br /> The base game makes it nearly impossible to start with overqualified PCs with the base stats &amp; skill spread.<br /> <br /> Originally, coming from a DnD background in which the games put a hard cap on your capacity based on your progression, which CofD doesn't do, I often have to remind some of my players, and sometimes even myself, that we play characters that are within human standards and 4 to 5 dots in a skill is pretty exceptional. When left unchecked, that causes tonal clashes with the tone of my campaigns.<br /> <br /> Hell, even 2 dots is assumed to be professional training.<br /> <br /> CoD character creation gives you the illusion that you can build a relatively normal character you could meet on the street, like \u2018\u2019a bored medical student\u2019\u2019 or a \u2018\u2019single parent trying to get by\u2019\u2019 but honestly\u2026 Unless those two have exceptionally well-hidden skills, you won\u2019t succeed at creating them without being at least overskilled in one area or two.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tangent about recreating myself as a CofD Character.</b><br /> More than a decade ago, something that got weirdly popular for a little while in my gaming circle was to recreate ourselves for a chronicle.<br /> I\u2019m under no illusion that I would ever get close to the power level of a CoD PC, but if I were to try to approximate my lived experience, I don\u2019t think I could even spend all attribute dots.<br /> Maybe I could justify intelligence 3 and resolve 3 to fully spend my 5 dots on mental attributes, but I\u2019m not fully convinced.<br /> And I certainly don\u2019t think I would ever qualify for more than 2 dots in a single skill. Let\u2019s take a look.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Academics :</b> I have a bachelor\u2019s degree, but I never been a PHD student. That\u2019s between 1 and 2 dots. 1 dot with some specialties might be more accurate.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Politics :</b> I can justify 1 dot, since I\u2019m keyed into most political issues in my area and did some political philosophy classes when I was at uni. And I work in a corporate environment; I can somewhat navigate the corporate office structure with relative success. I simply choose not to do so because I hate it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other mental skills :</b> At most hobby skills, as a millennial, I could justify not having a penalty on computer skills, but I certainly do not have any programmation skills to justify 1 dot. </span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drive :</b> One of the rare physical skills I could justify, but only since I know how to drive in the snow as a Canadian and I\u2019ve successfully dodged 2 very risky scenarios that could have got me killed. (Or I could have been super lucky with my chance die, twice! It was pretty scary).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Weaponry :</b> The only other physical skill I could justify, as I played larp a lot back in my younger days, I could justify one dot, or buy off the penalty. I haven't played in a while; I\u2019m pretty rusty, not going to lie. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other physical skills :</b> Maybe I could justify not having a penalty on athletics, since I\u2019ve been trekking a bit lately, but I\u2019m not constantly playing sports. I\u2019m above the North American average, but that\u2019s not saying much, to be honest.</span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Empathy :</b> I think could justify 2 dots. I had some social working classes and worked part-time in a youth centre for a few years and I work in public. That makes you pick up social cues pretty quickly.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Expression:</b> I've dabble in a few artistic hobbies. As a virtue of being really invested into roleplay, i could justify 1 dot.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other Social Skills :</b> I might be able to justify 1 dot in most social skills as a virtue of working in public and living downtown and I have a general knack for at least \u2018\u2019belonging\u2019\u2019 in a social setting, but that\u2019s about it. Intimidation would be a stretch, Animal Ken is definitely out of the window. </span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a generous interpretation, that would leave me around roughly 11 to 10 unspent skill dots of 22. With generous interpretation, I might be able to spend all my attribute points, with something like Intelligence 3, wits 2, Resolve 3, all physical 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 3, and Composure 2.<br /> Damn, I\u2019m an NPC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think the difficulty of creating a grounded character in CofD comes from the assumption that the game runs on movie/book logic, rather than realistic assumptions. The game is viewed through the lens of chapters &amp; scenes. In books and movie characters tend to be generally skilled, unless their incompetence is a plot point.<br /> That being said, that\u2019s for PCs, and NPCs generally shouldn\u2019t follow PC creation rules.<br /> In the case of Isabel &amp; Isiah, I will admit some of their skill dots are a bit eyebrow raising. With as little context as I\u2019m provided, I would probably change the following both characters :<br /> <b>Isobel : </b>I will assume that she mostly lives on the streets, in a dangerous city.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes :</b> Strength 2, dex 3, stamina 1, rest is fine.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mental : </b>Craft 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Science 1</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Physical :</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Firearms 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 1</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Social : </b>Empathy 2, Intimidation 3, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 2</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Merit : </b>I\u2019d go with contacts in the underworld, allies, etc. Striking look 2 is high, but it doesn\u2019t necessarily mean hot; she could be intimidating.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternatively : </b>make her older and she could be a vet that ended up on the streets, a sadly too-common fate, that would probably justify her high firearm skills.<br /> <br /> <b>Isaah :</b> As others have mentioned, his expressive skill + specialty in acting is odd for a failed actor, but he could be failed because of multiple reasons. Skill is not a guaranteed factor of success; unfortunately, plenty of people succeed because they are well connected and plenty of skilled people do not because they never had the chance to prove themselves. Hopefully for him, he can fix that in the future when someone realizes his talent.<br /> As for using autobuilder, that\u2019s\u2026 certainly a choice. It will leave you with oddities for your NPC concept. Not to tell you what to do, but you don\u2019t need to build a full sheet for an NPC if you lack the time to do so. Some simple writeups like the NPC you can find in the core books are detailed enough.<br /> <br /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T01:56:33-07:00","id":1564882,"title":"","content":"The thing isn't just that the game works on movie/book logic, but a related yet slightly distinct fact: it's about exceptional people.<br /> <br /> Stories are about exceptional people. CoD isn't about making ordinary characters, it's about making <i>exceptional grounded characters</i>. Looks the same, but isn't. A character with Science 4 isn't a regular person, is an exceptional person you have the reference to understand within a grounded context.<br /> <br /> We have a tendency of assuming the character creation rules generate a weak beginner. There are several reasons: is the baseline we actually experience, is the baseline we share with other players, looking at other chronicles/characters give the impression that those are common within the game world, and our eyes set into the promises of advancement make the initial state seems weak.<br /> <br /> In a sense it even is, as stories are also about exceptional circumstances that will challenge those exceptional people beyond their already impressive feats.<br /> <br /> Not just a CoD problem, either. It's easy to forget in D&amp;D that your 1st level adventurer is already stronger than 90% of the population. Your regular farmer has between 8 and 13 in each Ability Score, average 10,5 and has no special ability. That's the baseline the story is made to assume (authors committing similar mistakes compound the problem in every game).<br /> <br /> Another thing most players and many STs don't get is that NPCs can freely use rules that are minor for PCs. CoD has Specializations and Merits and rules to invest on them, reaching higher stats without investing in the Skill directly.<br /> <br /> For a PC, with a player thinking in terms of point cost, it's mostly meant for special cases or to hit above the trait limits. But for NPCs? A big chunk of them probably don't have a single Skill above 1, rather having specializations that allow the professional levels in whatever they actually do.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, not many professionals, even exceptional ones, are absurdly skilled in every single natural science known to humanity or every manual skill whatsoever.<br /> <hr /><br /> NPCs rarely need more than two or three stats. I give them a few more just in case I need to rule through weird player decisions, but overall even that won't extend beyond 7, 10 if you want to be absolutely thorough on derived traits and resources.<br /> <hr /><br /> Isabel and Isaiah could be explained out with little effort and no change to traits if they were treated as actual people, even if NPCs, rather than shallow stereotypes, and keeping the concepts to boot.<br /> <br /> Being a veteran would help a lot with Isabel, but she could also be genuinely an exceptional gang member that nonetheless get shit because she's a woman.<br /> <br /> There are gang members that, upon raising by being better at something, do start to learn other things as they are, you know, people. Also sometimes college students and even young professionals get down on their luck enough to end up in such a wasted state.<br /> <br /> She's good looking, given the actual benefits I don't buy Striking Looks as being an intimidating presence, although it really doesn't have to mean beautiful, just pleasing to be around. There's a lot to explore there and then how she ended where she is.<br /> <br /> For Isaiah I can easily picture someone who was really good in theater school, talented and promising, yet simply pushed by sabotage from more powerful people fearing competition, and then his life starts to go bad very intensely and fast.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, the very stereotypes could have been relied upon without flattening. She IS a Chicana and he IS black, and plenty of bad stuff happen to those people in the US because of prejudice and racism.<br /> <br /> Which is precisely the ignored reason why they are disproportionately found on such situations for real.<br /> <hr /><br /> Anyway I'm half curious, half dreading how Iguazu would react if he saw the color of my skin, or if my country already colors his reactions.<br /> <br /> Not saying it does, just that I wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T10:19:32-07:00","id":1564897,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While certainly common, stories are not exclusively about exceptional people; they can also be about exceptional situations. In my French literature classes back at university, we read a lot of books with very mundane protagonists with no particular set skills worth mentioning. Very often they would actually be worse than average and that's what made the story interesting.<br /> <br /> RPGs, including CofD, will often focus on action/pulp style, or generally skilled protagonists. For multiple reasons; I suspect that it makes for easier storytelling and players would rather play skilled characters than mundane corporate office clerks. Stories also tend to come to a halt when a player fails and they usually run for longer than a book or a movie by \u2018\u2019content length\u2019\u2019, at least it\u2019s true in my case.<br /> That being said, I don\u2019t disagree with your assessment.<br /> <br /> We can also agree or disagree on whatever a grounded exceptional character means, but my initial perception of the game was definitely skewed toward understanding starting the character as barely above average. However erroneous that might be, for the simple fact that the first character examples that are given are \u2018\u2019single mother scrapping by\u2019\u2019 and \u2018\u2019bored medical students\u2019\u2019. My introduction to the game certainly had more of a street-level feel to it too.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t lie; coming from DnD probably skewed my perception as well.<br /> <br /> However, I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s possible to truly end up with a bored medical student who also won\u2019t be a genius or very skilled at a collection of skills, in a way that makes them formidable in their own right. Not to downplay motherhood, as all single mothers are their own version of badass, but a CofD version of that \u2018\u2019archetype\u2019\u2019, for lack of a better word, will also be better than average.<br /> <br /> I, personally, don\u2019t see that as particularly grounded. They are simply less fantastical or exceptional than most rpg characters at first glance.<br /> <br /> Like most point-buy games I've played, the game doesn\u2019t hold the player and the storyteller by the hand. Any questions of relevance and justification are purely left to the player and story teller\u2019s discretion.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Does my character, who hunts twice a year, really have that many dots in firearms? </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Does my medical student character really have much more than one dot in medicine? </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But if they don\u2019t, won\u2019t that make them much more spectacular in another field diluting the whole concept\u2026</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are no inherent guard rails, which aren\u2019t necessarily a bad thing, but it\u2019s especially made worse by the fact that all traits have a flat XP cost. I very much disagree that the difference in the efficiency of resources 2 and 5 is worth 3 XP, but I\u2019ll cut myself there, as I\u2019m already pretty far into that tangent.<br /> <br /> You are also right; skills are very versatile. One has to interpret the game\u2019s skills as an approximation of real life abilities and roleplay and interpretation has to fill in the blank if they wish for an experience that's closer to reality. An expression 5 world-renowned fantasy writers can technically play piano like Bethoven, but it doesn\u2019t mean that the player and storyteller can\u2019t stop for a second to ask themselves if it makes sense given the character and the type of story. That\u2019s the price to pay to avoid having a crazy amount of skill lists like GURPS.<br /> <br /> Fact is\u2026 It\u2019s pretty hard to make a struggling down to earth character. You have to really restrain yourself and think in advance, or they will end up ridiculously overskilled in an area or two. I wish the game had a weaker starting character with a clearer XP bracket for the style of campaign one would like to run. As I, personally, find it very fun to play regular folk in difficult situations, I often find myself distancing myself from characters that are too exceptional. </span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For NPCs stats block complexity. I actually agree; full sheets aren't necessary. I\u2019m a bit crazy and I like to make the full sheet because I run a sandbox game, but that\u2019s only for what I\u2019d categorize as NPCs rather than extras.<br /> <br /> In my games, NPCs have goals that go further than the immediate and while they certainly do not receive as much spotlight as players, they have agency and will not only react but also act. I design NPCs in a way that a player could technically take control of their sheets and read their background and I\u2019d trust the player to actively be able to pick up and do a fairly good job at portraying them.<br /> Extras are people I create on the spot for a scene, or cheap antagonists, like cops, gangsters for an action scene. That won\u2019t deserve the full attention of an NPC as they will most likely never be relevant beyond that one scene they appeared in, unless players become very fond of the personality I created on the fly for some reason. For those I generally make a dice pool on the spot ranging from 2 to 6 based on what feels right. </span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Isabel and Isaiah, yeah, the descriptions provided were certainly too short to humanize them.<br /> <br /> For Isabella, I was mostly trying to charitably make sense of the sheet or the character concept, which clearly appears to have some inherent dichotomy that needs explanation.<br /> <br /> I agree that she could be a skilled gang member, but it would be weird for her to have streetwise 1, which would be a skill she would most likely use all the time as a gang member and have a nearly world class elite assassins skill in weaponry and firearms. This, to me, screams more \u2018\u2019Someone recently down on their luck\u2019\u2019 than \u2018\u2019Hardened gang member\u2019\u2019.<br /> <br /> As for striking looks, are you talking about Isabela\u2019s case or striking look in general? Because the striking look merit does include ''repulsive'' and ''commanding'' which aren\u2019t what I\u2019d call pleasant. In Isabella\u2019s case, given that we\u2019re only given a hero\u2019s forge miniature to judge, I don\u2019t know. A homeless person or a drug addict can appear intimidating in their mannerisms and appearance, in the sense that they make most people feel uncomfortable. (For numerous reasons that aren't really their fault.)<br /> <br /> That being said, you\u2019re more keyed in than I am on the stereotype as a French Canadian and I can certainly see how the concept comes across as offensive. I\u2019m not as alert to that kind of stereotypification as you are, as I\u2019m not dealing with it on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m reminded of Elizabeth Anderson\u2019s book <i>The Imperative of Integration, </i>which aptly describes the issues with the colour-blind approach; namely that it obfuscates sources of inequality and oppression. The conclusion of her book was\u2026 debatable if not maybe a bit clumsy in some aspects, but that\u2019s another subject.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You\u2019d think I would be shielded from racism and sexism with my white and male privileges, but those folks often get too comfortable telling me what they should keep to themselves.<br /> <br /> The other day at work, I had an elderly lady complain to me that the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is a holiday to honour the native residential school survivors &amp; victims, was going too far, as \u2018\u2019We already did enough for them.\u2019\u2019<br /> <br /> Always awkward when behind the counter to have to politely explain that no, actually, it\u2019s the bare minimum we can do.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not having it nearly as bad as those that are actively oppressed, but it is an annoying side of looking like the in-group sometimes.<br /> <br /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T14:51:18-07:00","id":1564900,"title":"","content":"Here's the King of the Homeless: He's more annoying that anything else. He was an ER Nurse, born in Germany. Maybe he was a student that overstayed. He speaks perfect English, except at times, his accent comes out. He drinks heavily and is up all night. <br /> <br /> <img width=\"1578\" height=\"1053\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://iili.io/nO0sQoX.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://iili.io/nO0sQoX.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://iili.io/nO0sQoX.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564849#post1564849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You made a thread for NPC writeups where a large part of the NPC writeup, the dot spreads, are randomly generated rather than something you actually wrote to fit them?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Each one takes over an hour or so. I used the app to produce some dots, then, I modify them according to the concept I have. I use, like, three computers, because my main one, doesn't like PDFs so I have to go to my older one and then I use my desktop because it has Adobe for the NPC-images; I use Mr. Gone's to fill in the dots. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T19:01:55-07:00","id":1564905,"title":"","content":"Stories about really average/close to average people are good, but not a standard for the types of stories a TTRPG tells more easily. Not without reason, games really geared for this kind of story are usually very specific for them.<br /> <br /> But in this case, it's just a matter of Character Creation rules, and I agree that the game could give an alternative low point system. It's feasible, but would require a very different approach to play.<br /> <br /> Probably I'd do something limiting the number of Attributes at 3, forbidding 4 or 5, for skills it's only 1 dot, then be a bit more generous with Specializations and Skill-related Merits. From this starting point I'd recalculate starting dots.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the problem with the Striking Looks + Street Kid + Spanish in the US is that this is squarely the &quot;Hot Chicana&quot; stereotype that's a disgusting sexualization of mixed Americans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T23:57:54-07:00","id":1564907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564897#post1564897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fact is\u2026 It\u2019s pretty hard to make a struggling down to earth character. You have to really restrain yourself and think in advance, or they will end up ridiculously overskilled in an area or two. I wish the game had a weaker starting character with a clearer XP bracket for the style of campaign one would like to run. As I, personally, find it very fun to play regular folk in difficult situations, I often find myself distancing myself from characters that are too exceptional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest just changing what the dots represent. Like, 1 dot stays the same, 3 dots uses the 2 dot description and 5 the 3. If a player wants to represent higher skill, then you have specialties, area of expertise, and the thing the charts really ignore: Professional Training. Like, the core might say that a character with 5 dots in Science is our era's Einstein, but that's not how it really works mechanically. A character with 3 Science and 5 Professional Training is going to be far more impactful on the game.<br /> <br /> The problem with making the stats lower is that you're going to have to offer a lot more bonus dice to avoid the game grinding to a halt from constant failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-22T06:58:56-07:00","id":1564909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564907#post1564907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with making the stats lower is that you're going to have to offer a lot more bonus dice to avoid the game grinding to a halt from constant failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually the point, getting more bonus dice.<br /> <br /> Seriously, what PCs do most of the time? They do stuff on the spot with whatever is around. Frequently they do really hard stuff like that.<br /> <br /> What do regular people do?<br /> <br /> 1. They stick to doing things they know how to;<br /> <br /> 2. They do their things properly equipped and in a properly prepared environment;<br /> <br /> 3. They stack the advantages they can;<br /> <br /> 4. Or else they either achieve a poor result, a really easy task still with difficulty, or just fail.<br /> <br /> In a game of common people, the point already is to feel they're common, not hiper-resourceful and doing crazy stuff.<br /> <br /> Current rules already afford for quite a lot. Let's say you have an Attribute at 2, skill at 1 + Specialization, a properly equipped workshop and specific tools for the exact craft you're doing, this is at least a combined +2 equipment bonus.<br /> <br /> You got 6 dice. That's an average 2 successes per roll for tasks you have to roll at all. Chance of failure small even if not negligible.<br /> <br /> And what are you rolling for? The last thing is to remember what kind of tasks even should require a roll at all, or receive a bonus because of being particularly easy. This isn't necessarily the ST giving more bonuses, although that can happen, but the players staying within simpler actions they know they can succeed easily, which is the actual point.<br /> <br /> Giving more dots for a given description risks being self-defeating: you have characters that are nominally weaker doing cinematic stuff and being over competent at everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-22T09:50:41-07:00","id":1564910,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">For character creation and progression I remade XP cost, all but merit now cost incremental XP. At the top of my head, the XP costs are :</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Attribute or disciplines :</b> New Dot x2</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Out of clan disciplines :</b> (new dot x2 )+2 </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Skills :</b> New Dot +1</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Merits :</b> 1 per dot</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Supernatural tolerance</b> 3 x New dot</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Characters start with 140 total XP and must buy everything from scratch with only 1 dot in all attributes and 1 dot in supernatural tolerance if it applies. This gives roughly the same XP as a CofD starting character, with the exception that dots above 3 are pretty expensive at creation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"> I could also lower starting XP if I wanted to have less exceptional character, i'd have to recalculate what would feel appropriate, but going of vibes, i feel like 120 wouldn't be too bad. </span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I also do agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> solution. I usually recontextualize a bit what dots will mean within the context of the game. Professional training, areas of expertise, and cross-disciplinary specialties are all wonderful merits to achieve greater specialties.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Interpreting dice results in the context of the setting environment rather than trying to fight the game system too hard is usually my preferred method. It\u2019s also, I think, more fun for players to have dots; they can increase in skill. Character mechanical progression is also valued in our circle.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Monteparnas is not wrong; however,the system already accounts for this using equipment.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">However, I\u2019m not a super fan of equipment beyond the odd circumstancial bonus. Indeed I found the equipment bonus to be really high when mixed with the starting character competencies. Penalties being capped at 5 also means that basic equipment + willpower trivialize the hardest checks. At 2 merely 2 dice, a character already crosses the 50% chance of success.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I think cash as social equipment is the most egregious case. For 5 XP spent on dots of resources, a character can spam +3 social equipment for free. To be fair, this is consistent with reality; money is indeed quite OP.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I\u2019m going to stop myself there. I\u2019ve already derailed the thread enough and I made it clear enough. I have some grievances with the base dice system, even though I quite like the game\u2019s overall structure. Hell, this is what inspired me to design my own game and even then I always come back to it in some fashion, so CofD is clearly doing something right in my book. </span> <hr /><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">, as for the harmful stereotype, that\u2019s unfortunate. I hope it\u2019s involuntary on Iguazu\u2019s part. I try to stay charitable but that\u2019s easy to say when I\u2019m so far removed. </span> <hr /><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2521_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2521\" data-vbnamecard=\"2521\">Iguazu</a> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"> your computer juggling sounds painful and time consuming.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Why generate random dots if you modify them after? Do you use this as a way to come up with an idea? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">If not, why not simply assign them dots how you see fit? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I personally use a word document with tables I organized to look into a character sheet for NPCs with space for their character image, connections &amp; backstory. This allows me to have all my NPCs in one big folder. I find it easier to manage than 150 PDFs (I\u2019m not exaggerating what I say 150 NPCS).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">For a quick generation, I also made myself a table with a dot budget, with specialist or generalist stats &amp; skill spreads. Sometimes, I also just go by feeling.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-22T19:27:45-07:00","id":1564918,"title":"","content":"Here's Joe Grubb (A real piece of shit): he's, &quot;Heir&quot;, to the Grubb-fortune; or maybe he's been disinherited: His sister supports him at times, especially when he needs his fix. He steals everything. From anyone. He also thinks he's a ladies-man and will hit on women. He knows Isi and they sometimes get a motel-room and do drugs together.<br /> <br /> Edit: he should have a lot more XP, but, he doesn't really need it. <br /> <br /> <img width=\"1575\" height=\"1123\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://iili.io/nexaqas.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://iili.io/nexaqas.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://iili.io/nexaqas.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":". 10-22-2026, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-22T19:51:33-07:00","id":1564919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564829-victims-aren-t-we-all?p=1564871#post1564871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Alternatively : </b>make her older and she could be a vet that ended up on the streets, a sadly too-common fate, that would probably justify her high firearm skills.<br /> <br /> <b>Isaah :</b> As others have mentioned, his expressive skill + specialty in acting is odd for a failed actor, but he could be failed because of multiple reasons. Skill is not a guaranteed factor of success; unfortunately, plenty of people succeed because they are well connected and plenty of skilled people do not because they never had the chance to prove themselves. Hopefully for him, he can fix that in the future when someone realizes his talent.<br /> As for using autobuilder, that\u2019s\u2026 certainly a choice. It will leave you with oddities for your NPC concept. Not to tell you what to do, but you don\u2019t need to build a full sheet for an NPC if you lack the time to do so. Some simple writeups like the NPC you can find in the core books are detailed enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pictured Isiah as an older black-man, but, I'm still learning the program and I should have aged him up to around 50ish; he's just based off his quote, hence the flashlight. For failing at acting. Maybe he rolled all ones or there were just better people at the auditions or his vice got in the way. There are very few people that want to work as a security-guard, at night, in the ghetto. <br /> <br /> Isi's firearm-skill is moot. She's too doped up to use it. When she sobers up enough to move, she's gotta get her next fix before withdrawal sets in and she gets dope-sick and sleeps all day. I say, she's just talented with a firearm. And if she does manage to use it against a vamp., won't they be surprised. <br /> <br /> And Joe Grubb WILL use her looks and pimp her out for money or drugs, claiming to be her, &quot;Friend&quot;, if she's not using him as well to get her fix. It works both ways. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-24T14:27:12-07:00","id":1564949,"title":"","content":"Here's Julia Grubb, Joe Grubb's sister and heir to the Grubb-forutune; she helps her brother out and sometimes, he helps her out with her real-estate, &quot;Deals&quot;. She's very ambitious and wants to become wealthy, without her family-name. The only reason she'd be out at night is for her brother. Very few of her real-estate-deals are at night. <img width=\"1610\" height=\"1060\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/Xn5mYtR1/Julia-Grubb.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/Xn5mYtR1/Julia-Grubb.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/Xn5mYtR1/Julia-Grubb.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T13:33:45-07:00","id":1564982,"title":"","content":"Here's Bob Grubb and his Butler/Caretaker, Brad. Grubb is a millionaire and rarely leaves the Estates. Brad manages the affairs of his household as well. Bob's retainer is Brad and Brad's mentor is Bob. Joe, thinks Brad might be trying to steal his fortune, but that's not the case; Brad, is still honest with his mortality intact. The Rose family are another group of millionaires that owns a factory(ies). For what language Brad spoke, I wanted him to be European or something, so I pulled out my Cyberpunk:2020 book and rolled; he got American-Spanish. Grubb is well-connected with the state and the police. <br /> <br /> <img width=\"2246\" height=\"1058\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://iili.io/nv3kS14.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://iili.io/nv3kS14.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://iili.io/nv3kS14.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"